  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 99,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.056,
            0.471,
            0.073
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "§8. An Application: Runge's Theorem"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.844,
            0.056,
            0.87,
            0.071
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "85"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.1,
            0.586,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is not difficult to see that for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } \\backslash K"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.126,
            0.677,
            0.17
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_99_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{d}{dw} \\right)^n \\hat{\\mu}(w_0) = n! \\int (z - w_0)^{-n-1} d\\mu(z)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.178,
            0.867,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, we can easily find the power series expansion of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at infinity. Indeed,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.204,
            0.719,
            0.248
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_99_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\hat { \\mu } ( w ) = \\int \\frac { 1 } { z - w } d \\mu ( z ) = - \\frac { 1 } { w } \\int \\left( 1 - \\frac { z } { w } \\right) ^ { - 1 } d \\mu ( z ) ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.257,
            0.799,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose w near enough to infinity that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "| z / w | < 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for all "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "z"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in K. Then"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.345,
            0.166,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.36,
            0.283,
            0.636,
            0.377
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_99_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{align*}\\hat{\\mu}(w) = & - \\frac{1}{w} \\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} \\int \\left( \\frac{z}{w} \\right)^n d\\mu(z) \\\\= & - \\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} \\frac{a_n}{w^{n + 1}},\\end{align*}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.375,
            0.324,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a _ { n } = \\int z ^ { n } d \\mu ( z ) ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.394,
            0.869,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now assume "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mu { \\in } M ( K )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\int   g   d \\mu = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for every rational function "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with poles in E. Let U be a component of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } _ { \\infty } \\backslash K ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { 0 } { \\in } E \\cap U"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { 0 } \\neq \\infty"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then the hypothesis and (8.3) imply that each derivative of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " vanishes. Hence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu } \\equiv 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on U. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { 0 } = \\infty"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then (8.4) implies "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu } \\equiv 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on U. Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu } \\equiv 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { C } _ { \\infty } \\backslash K"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.487,
            0.869,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If f is analytic on an open set G containing K, let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\gamma _ { 1 } , \\ldots , \\gamma _ { n }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be straight-line segments in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "G \\backslash K"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.364,
            0.527,
            0.627,
            0.571
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_99_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "f(z) = \\sum_{k = 1}^{n} \\frac{1}{2\\pi i} \\int_{\\gamma_{k}} \\frac{f(w)}{w - z} dw"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.577,
            0.636,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "for all "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "z"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in K. (See p. 195 of Conway [1978].) Thus"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.292,
            0.603,
            0.702,
            0.697
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_99_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{align*}\\int_{K} f(z) d\\mu(z) &= \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\frac{1}{2\\pi i} \\int_{K} \\int_{\\gamma_k} \\frac{f(w)}{w-z} dw d\\mu(z) \\\\&= - \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\frac{1}{2\\pi i} \\int_{\\gamma_k} f(w) \\hat{\\mu}(w) dw\\end{align*}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.703,
            0.868,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "by Fubini's Theorem. But "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu } ( w ) = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\gamma _ { k } ~ ( \\in \\pmb { \\mathbb { C } } \\backslash K )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " so "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\int f   d \\mu = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " By (6.13), "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f   \\in   R ( K , E )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This proves Runge's Theorem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.755,
            0.87,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.5. Corollary. If K is compact and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } \\backslash K"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is connected and if f is analytic in a neighborhood of K, then there is a sequence of polynomials that converges to f uniformly on K."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.828,
            0.231,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "EXERCISES"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.848,
            0.868,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mu"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be a compactly supported measure on C that is boundedly absolutely continuous with respect to area measure. Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mu }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is continuous on "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { C } _ { \\infty } ,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.89,
            0.869,
            0.925
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Let m = Lebesgue measure on [0, 1]. Show that m is not continuous at any point of [0, 1]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
